this is omens new sultan Haytham ban  tariq al saeed sworn in a few hours  after the death of his predecessor  sultan qaboos the oldest ruling monarch  in the region and the founding father of  modern day oh man sultan - made it clear  in his first speech to the public that  he will follow in the footsteps of the  late sultan we remain guided by the late  Sultan's wisdom going forward we will  preserve and embark on the achievements  he made this is what we are adamant to  do to follow in his footsteps with  respect to international relations  we will follow in the same course set  out by the late Sultan we will embrace  foreign policies based on peaceful  coexistence without any interference in  domestic affairs of other states the  succession ceremony was swift and smooth  dispelling any concerns about  uncertainty and instability in one of  the oldest dynasties in the Gulf region  the new Sultan will have several roles  he is the prime minister controls the  government the Armed Forces finance and  foreign affairs his biggest challenge is  balancing a budget that relies on  revenues from dwindling gas and oil  resources the death of Sultan Qaboos  comes at a critical moment tension has  grown in the region after the u.s.  assassination of Iranian military  commander Qasem Soleimani  his killing has shattered any hopes of a  diplomatic solution no man has in the  past played a crucial role in narrowing  differences between the two rivals it  has a long-standing neutral approach to  the problems of the region in 2017 when  Saudi Arabia the UAE Egypt and Bahrain  imposed a blockade or utter o man  refused to take sides calling instead  for dialogue it also plays a central  role in the international efforts and  the war in Yemen  the new sultan has insisted he will  maintain his nations neutrality and  honor the legacy of sultan qaboos the  late ruler came to power in 1970 at a  time when a man was underdeveloped  divided and facing a rebellion in the  South but caboose managed to overcome  those obstacles and turn it into a  modern state caboose faced another  challenge in 2011 when thousands of  people protested demanding better wages  and more jobs as the Arab Spring was  spreading Sultan Qaboos fired members of  his government gave more powers to the  consultative council and began reforming  the public sector the late one arc will  be remembered by his people as a  unifying figure and by the world as a  shrewd politician who turned a small  nation into a regional player Hashim  Espada al Jazeera
 

